// Layer contract for the expression pipeline, read top to bottom: the
// evaluator reduces a tree to a value, the formatter spells one back
// out as text, the parser runs the conversion that produces one, the
// syntax tree is what it hands back, the lexer
// feeds it, tokens are what the lexer emits, and errors sit beneath all
// of them because any stage may fail. A module may reach downward and
// nowhere else, so each entry lists the layers open to it and every
// other crate path is refused.
//
// Two layers stand over that pipeline and three off to the side. A
// table of values already worked out needs the evaluator to fill an
// entry and the formatter to name one, which puts it over both; the
// driver that hands subtrees to worker threads needs the table, which
// puts it over that. To the side sit the cell an entry is made of and
// the module naming the primitives the cell is built from, neither of
// which reaches into the pipeline at all, so they sit as low as the
// errors do. Beside those two sit the generators, which read three
// stages of the pipeline to build inputs for it and which nothing in
// the crate may read back.
//
// Naming what is open rather than what is shut is what makes this file
// carry cycle-freedom between the layers: every crate-internal import
// points down the order, and a set of modules whose edges all point one
// way cannot close a loop. cargo-modules offers a cycle check that
// would say the same from the other side, and 0.26.0 cannot say it: the
// search runs across the item graph before any filter narrows it, and a
// type owning a method that names the type back is a loop at that
// width. Every crate with an impl block fails it, so the reading lives
// here until the tool narrows first.
//
// Import paths are matched as they are written, so each pattern accepts
// both the `crate::` prefix the sources use and the crate's own name.
// A list of what is open has to name the standard library too, which
// the deeper layers reach for as freely as the rest, and has to leave
// room for the empty path an import reports for its own braces. Every
// name inside those braces arrives on its own and spelled out in full,
// which is where the reading happens. Each entry covers the module's
// submodules along with the file itself, a reach being a reach whatever
// depth it is written at. The evaluator is the exception, its one
// submodule standing a layer above it and answering to a rule of its
// own, so the pattern there stops at the file.
//
// A module with no entry here is not under the promise above, but
// nothing that is may import it, so it stays a leaf until someone
// writes its layer down. Two modules share one rung of the order: one
// reduces a tree to a value and one spells the same tree back out.
// Their lists are the same list and neither one appears in it, which
// is how the file says the readings are independent. One rule at the
// end runs the other way round, naming what is shut rather than what
// is open, because the module it shuts out has to stay shut to every
// module at once, including the ones nobody has written yet.
(
    lints: [
        Module((
            name: "driver_above_the_table",
            matches: Module("^proofhouse_rust_lib::evaluator::concurrent(::|$)"),
            rules: [
                // Splitting a tree across threads takes the node types
                // to walk, the table the threads meet in, the step
                // that joins two operand values under an operator, and
                // the failures any of that reports. The table is the
                // reason this sits at the top: whoever holds it holds
                // everything under it.
                RestrictImports(
                    allowed_only: Some([
                        "^(crate|proofhouse_rust_lib)::(ast|cache|errors|evaluator|parser)(::|$)",
                        "^std(::|$)",
                        "^$",
                    ]),
                    denied: None,
                    severity: Error,
                ),
            ],
        )),
        Module((
            name: "table_above_both_readings",
            matches: Module("^proofhouse_rust_lib::cache(::|$)"),
            rules: [
                // A key is a rendering and a value is a reduction, so
                // filling one entry takes both readings of a tree and
                // the table stands over the pair. The cell holding an
                // entry and the primitives behind the cell are open to
                // it as well, those sitting beside the errors rather
                // than anywhere in the pipeline.
                RestrictImports(
                    allowed_only: Some([
                        "^(crate|proofhouse_rust_lib)::(ast|errors|evaluator|formatter|parser)(::|$)",
                        "^(crate|proofhouse_rust_lib)::(sync|sync_shim)(::|$)",
                        "^std(::|$)",
                        "^$",
                    ]),
                    denied: None,
                    severity: Error,
                ),
            ],
        )),
        Module((
            name: "evaluator_over_the_parser",
            matches: Module("^proofhouse_rust_lib::evaluator$"),
            rules: [
                // Reducing a tree to a number takes the node types, a
                // way to get a tree out of text, and the failures
                // either step reports. Nothing above the parser is in
                // reach, and the formatter stands above the parser, so
                // no path from here arrives at a rendering. The table
                // is out of reach for the same reason read the other
                // way round: it is the table that calls this module.
                RestrictImports(
                    allowed_only: Some([
                        "^(crate|proofhouse_rust_lib)::(ast|parser|errors)(::|$)",
                        "^std(::|$)",
                        "^$",
                    ]),
                    denied: None,
                    severity: Error,
                ),
            ],
        )),
        Module((
            name: "formatter_beside_the_evaluator",
            matches: Module("^proofhouse_rust_lib::formatter(::|$)"),
            rules: [
                // Spelling a tree out reads the node types, and
                // checking that the spelling survives reads it back
                // through the parser. What the list withholds is the
                // module next door. A value and a rendering are two
                // readings of one tree taken from the pipeline they
                // share, so neither may arrive through the other, and
                // the omission on both sides is where that holds.
                RestrictImports(
                    allowed_only: Some([
                        "^(crate|proofhouse_rust_lib)::(ast|parser|errors)(::|$)",
                        "^std(::|$)",
                        "^$",
                    ]),
                    denied: None,
                    severity: Error,
                ),
            ],
        )),
        Module((
            name: "parser_above_everything",
            matches: Module("^proofhouse_rust_lib::parser(::|$)"),
            rules: [
                // The whole conversion runs from here, so every stage
                // beneath is in reach and the list is all of them.
                // What it turns away is a module nobody has placed
                // yet, which would leave the top of the pipeline
                // resting on something with no layer of its own.
                RestrictImports(
                    allowed_only: Some([
                        "^(crate|proofhouse_rust_lib)::(ast|lexer|tokens|errors)(::|$)",
                        "^std(::|$)",
                        "^$",
                    ]),
                    denied: None,
                    severity: Error,
                ),
            ],
        )),
        Module((
            name: "syntax_tree_below_the_parser",
            matches: Module("^proofhouse_rust_lib::ast(::|$)"),
            rules: [
                // A tree of nodes is a value like any other. Producing
                // one takes a lexer and a parser; being one takes
                // neither, and the reach that would make it otherwise
                // is what closes the pipeline into a loop. Errors stay
                // open because a node may carry the position a failure
                // points at.
                RestrictImports(
                    allowed_only: Some([
                        "^(crate|proofhouse_rust_lib)::errors(::|$)",
                        "^std(::|$)",
                        "^$",
                    ]),
                    denied: None,
                    severity: Error,
                ),
            ],
        )),
        Module((
            name: "lexer_below_the_syntax_tree",
            matches: Module("^proofhouse_rust_lib::lexer(::|$)"),
            rules: [
                // Scanning text into tokens is settled before a tree
                // exists, so the tokens it emits and the failures it
                // raises are the whole of what it needs. Reading the
                // tree or the parser from here would make the first
                // half of the pipeline depend on the second.
                RestrictImports(
                    allowed_only: Some([
                        "^(crate|proofhouse_rust_lib)::(tokens|errors)(::|$)",
                        "^std(::|$)",
                        "^$",
                    ]),
                    denied: None,
                    severity: Error,
                ),
            ],
        )),
        Module((
            name: "tokens_below_the_lexer",
            matches: Module("^proofhouse_rust_lib::tokens(::|$)"),
            rules: [
                // The token types describe what a lexer produces
                // without knowing that a lexer is what produces them,
                // which leaves errors the one layer beneath them.
                // Whoever writes the next producer inherits the same
                // freedom.
                RestrictImports(
                    allowed_only: Some([
                        "^(crate|proofhouse_rust_lib)::errors(::|$)",
                        "^std(::|$)",
                        "^$",
                    ]),
                    denied: None,
                    severity: Error,
                ),
            ],
        )),
        Module((
            name: "cell_beside_the_errors",
            matches: Module("^proofhouse_rust_lib::sync(::|$)"),
            rules: [
                // Publishing one value to whoever asks knows nothing
                // about expressions and never will: it holds a `T`.
                // The primitives it is built from are the one crate
                // path open to it, which is what leaves the cell
                // usable from any layer without carrying one along.
                RestrictImports(
                    allowed_only: Some([
                        "^(crate|proofhouse_rust_lib)::sync_shim(::|$)",
                        "^std(::|$)",
                        "^$",
                    ]),
                    denied: None,
                    severity: Error,
                ),
            ],
        )),
        Module((
            name: "primitives_below_the_cell",
            matches: Module("^proofhouse_rust_lib::sync_shim(::|$)"),
            rules: [
                // Naming a lock and an atomic is the whole of the job,
                // and the two places those names come from are the
                // standard library and the model runner that stands in
                // for it. A crate path here would put this module
                // above something, and the point of it is to sit under
                // everything that synchronizes.
                RestrictImports(
                    allowed_only: Some([
                        "^(std|loom)(::|$)",
                        "^$",
                    ]),
                    denied: None,
                    severity: Error,
                ),
            ],
        )),
        Module((
            name: "generators_beside_the_pipeline",
            matches: Module("^proofhouse_rust_lib::testing(::|$)"),
            rules: [
                // Building an input takes the node types to assemble,
                // the token record to fill, and the rendering that
                // turns a tree into text a reader accepts. What the
                // list withholds is every stage that consumes such an
                // input: a generator knowing what its output reduces
                // to would be free to hand back only the cases that
                // pass. The search library is the one path here from
                // outside the crate, and the feature gating this
                // module is what keeps it off an ordinary build.
                RestrictImports(
                    allowed_only: Some([
                        "^(crate|proofhouse_rust_lib)::(ast|formatter|tokens)(::|$)",
                        "^proptest(::|$)",
                        "^$",
                    ]),
                    denied: None,
                    severity: Error,
                ),
            ],
        )),
        Module((
            name: "errors_below_everything",
            matches: Module("^proofhouse_rust_lib::errors(::|$)"),
            rules: [
                // Every stage above reports failures through these
                // types, which leaves this module the one place with
                // no crate path open to it at all. An error type that
                // reached back for a token or a node would drag the
                // whole pipeline into whatever imports it.
                RestrictImports(
                    allowed_only: Some([
                        "^std(::|$)",
                        "^$",
                    ]),
                    denied: None,
                    severity: Error,
                ),
            ],
        )),
        Module((
            name: "no_stage_reaches_the_generators",
            matches: Module("^proofhouse_rust_lib(::|$)"),
            rules: [
                // Generators exist for the suites that drive this
                // crate from outside it. Every list above already
                // withholds them; this says so once for the whole
                // crate, so a module written later inherits the
                // refusal rather than waiting for someone to place it
                // in the order. An integration test compiles as its
                // own crate and so never meets this rule, which is
                // what leaves the suites free while the library stays
                // shut.
                RestrictImports(
                    allowed_only: None,
                    denied: Some([
                        "^(crate|proofhouse_rust_lib)::testing(::|$)",
                    ]),
                    severity: Error,
                ),
            ],
        )),
    ],
)
